# SafeArea

## 1. What is SafeArea?

`SafeArea` keeps your UI inside the **safe visible area of the screen**.

Modern phones can have:

* Notches
* Camera cutouts
* Status bars
* Rounded corners
* Bottom gesture/navigation areas

Without SafeArea, content can sometimes get too close to or underneath these areas.

---

# 2. Basic Example

```dart
SafeArea(
  child: Text(
    "Hello Flutter",
  ),
)
```

Usually:

```dart
Scaffold(
  body: SafeArea(
    child: Column(
      children: [
        Text("Welcome"),
        Text("Home Screen"),
      ],
    ),
  ),
)
```

---

# 3. Why Do We Need It?

Imagine your screen:

```text
┌─────────────────────┐
│ 📷  Status / Notch  │
├─────────────────────┤
│                     │
│     Your Content    │
│                     │
│                     │
├─────────────────────┤
│ Navigation Area     │
└─────────────────────┘
```

`SafeArea` keeps your content away from the unsafe edges.

---

# 4. Common Usage

A common screen structure is:

```dart
Scaffold(
  appBar: AppBar(
    title: Text("Home"),
  ),

  body: SafeArea(
    child: Column(
      children: [
        Text("Welcome"),
        SizedBox(height: 20),
        ElevatedButton(
          onPressed: () {},
          child: Text("Continue"),
        ),
      ],
    ),
  ),
)
```

---

# 5. SafeArea + Scrollable Content

For a long screen:

```dart
Scaffold(
  body: SafeArea(
    child: SingleChildScrollView(
      child: Column(
        children: [
          Text("Profile"),
          TextField(),
          TextField(),
          TextField(),
          ElevatedButton(
            onPressed: () {},
            child: Text("Save"),
          ),
        ],
      ),
    ),
  ),
)
```

The flow is:

```text
SafeArea
   ↓
SingleChildScrollView
   ↓
Column
   ↓
Content
```

---

# 6. SafeArea + ListView

For lists:

```dart
Scaffold(
  body: SafeArea(
    child: ListView.builder(
      itemCount: 50,
      itemBuilder: (context, index) {
        return ListTile(
          title: Text("Item $index"),
        );
      },
    ),
  ),
)
```

---

# 7. SafeArea Properties

You can control which sides are protected.

```dart
SafeArea(
  top: true,
  bottom: true,
  left: true,
  right: true,
  child: YourWidget(),
)
```

For example:

```dart
SafeArea(
  top: false,
  child: YourWidget(),
)
```

This means the top safe-area padding won't be applied.

Usually, you can simply use:

```dart
SafeArea(
  child: YourWidget(),
)
```

and let Flutter handle it.

---

# 8. SafeArea vs Padding

These are different.

### Padding

You decide the spacing:

```dart
Padding(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),
  child: Text("Hello"),
)
```

### SafeArea

Flutter protects the content from unsafe screen areas:

```dart
SafeArea(
  child: Text("Hello"),
)
```

You can also combine them:

```dart
SafeArea(
  child: Padding(
    padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),
    child: Text("Hello"),
  ),
)
```

Meaning:

```text
SafeArea
   ↓
Protect screen edges
   ↓
Padding
   ↓
Add your own spacing
   ↓
Content
```

---

# 9. SafeArea vs AppBar

If you use:

```dart
Scaffold(
  appBar: AppBar(...),
)
```

Flutter already handles the AppBar's placement around the system status area.

You generally don't need:

```dart
SafeArea(
  child: AppBar(...)
)
```

Instead, SafeArea is commonly useful for the **body/content** when needed.

---

# 10. Real Example — Login Screen

```dart
Scaffold(
  body: SafeArea(
    child: Padding(
      padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),

      child: Column(
        mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,

        children: [

          Text(
            "Login",
            style: TextStyle(
              fontSize: 30,
              fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
            ),
          ),

          SizedBox(height: 30),

          TextField(
            decoration: InputDecoration(
              labelText: "Email",
              border: OutlineInputBorder(),
            ),
          ),

          SizedBox(height: 15),

          TextField(
            obscureText: true,
            decoration: InputDecoration(
              labelText: "Password",
              border: OutlineInputBorder(),
            ),
          ),

          SizedBox(height: 20),

          SizedBox(
            width: double.infinity,
            child: ElevatedButton(
              onPressed: () {},
              child: Text("Login"),
            ),
          ),
        ],
      ),
    ),
  ),
)
```

---

# 11. Easy Memory

```text
SafeArea
    ↓
Protect UI from
notch / status bar /
navigation area
```

### Remember:

```text
SafeArea
    = safe screen boundaries

Padding
    = your own spacing

Expanded
    = use available space

Flexible
    = use available space without forcing full size
```
